        <h1>Chapter 1: Prose, Typography &amp; Inline Mathematics</h1>
        
        <level2>
          <h2>1.1 Semantic Text &amp; Typeforms</h2>
          <p>
            This paragraph illustrates full typography support under BANA and UEB formatting standards.
            Words can have <strong>bold emphasis</strong>, <em>italic emphasis</em>, or <span class="underline">underline styling</span>.
            Multiple typeforms can also be combined such as <strong><em>bold italicized terms</em></strong>.
          </p>
        </level2>

        <level2>
          <h2>1.2 Inline and Display Mathematics (MathML 3)</h2>
          <p>
            Mathematical expressions are encoded with standard W3C MathML:
            The quadratic formula is represented as 
            <m:math display="inline" alttext="x = \frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}" altimg="images/math-quadratic-formula.png">
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>=</m:mo>
              <m:mfrac>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                  <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                  <m:mo>±</m:mo>
                  <m:msqrt>
                    <m:mrow>
                      <m:msup><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup>
                      <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                      <m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mi>c</m:mi>
                    </m:mrow>
                  </m:msqrt>
                </m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mi>a</m:mi>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mfrac>
            </m:math>, 
            and the Pythagorean identity is <m:math display="inline" alttext="a^2 + b^2 = c^2" altimg="images/math-pythagorean-identity.png"><m:msup><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>b</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:msup><m:mi>c</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:math>.
          </p>

          <div class="doc-break">
            <p class="break">⁂ ⁂ ⁂</p>
          </div>
        </level2>
      </level1>

