        <h1>Chapter 3: Plays, Poetry, Annotations &amp; Transcriber Notes</h1>

        <level2>
          <h2>3.1 Drama &amp; Dialogue (BANA §13)</h2>
          <div class="dialogue">
            <p class="stage"><em>[Setting: A high terrace overlooking the ocean at sunset. Enter ELENA and MARCUS.]</em></p>
            <p class="speaker"><strong>ELENA:</strong> Have you observed the navigation stars tonight? The horizon is completely clear.</p>
            <p class="speaker"><strong>MARCUS:</strong> <em>(Consulting the marine astrolabe)</em> The coordinates align precisely with the northern chart.</p>
            <p class="stage"><em>[He marks the parchment chart with a brass compass.]</em></p>
          </div>
        </level2>

        <level2>
          <h2>3.2 Poetry &amp; Stanza Layout (BANA §13)</h2>
          <poem>
            <linegroup>
              <line>The tide retreats across the silver sand,</line>
              <line>Leaving smooth echoes where the breakers rolled;</line>
              <line>Night casts its quiet shadow on the land,</line>
              <line>And turns the ocean foam to gleaming gold.</line>
            </linegroup>
          </poem>
        </level2>

